{{was wotd|2007|April|30}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|NL.|en}} *{{term||differentiatus}}, past participle of *{{term||differentiare}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|differentia||difference|lang=la}}; see [[difference]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪf.əˈrɛn.ʃi.eɪt/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˌdɪ.fəˈrɛnt.ʃi.eɪt/}}
* {{audio|en-us-differentiate.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|differentiat|ing}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[show]], or be the [[distinction]] between two things.
#* Earle
#*: The word "then" was '''differentiated''' into the two forms "then" and "than".
#* {{quote-book|year=1933
|passage=The mass of the rich and poor are '''differentiated''' by their incomes and nothing else, and the average millionaire is only the average dishwasher dressed in a new suit.
|author=George Orwell|title=Down and Out in Paris and London|chapter=Ch. XXII|page=120|publisher=Harvest / Harcourt paperback edition}}
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To [[perceive]] the [[difference]] between things; to [[discriminate]].
#* {{quote-book|title=[[S:New York Times v. Sullivan|New York Times v. Sullivan]]|year=1964
|passage=he refused to instruct that actual intent to harm or recklessness had to be found before punitive damages could be awarded, or that a verdict for respondent should '''differentiate''' between compensatory and punitive damages.}}
# {{context|transitive|intransitive|lang=en}} To [[modify]], or be [[modified]].
# {{context|transitive|mathematics|lang=en}} To [[calculate]] the [[derivative]] of a [[function]].
# {{context|transitive|mathematics|lang=en}} To calculate the [[differential]] of a function of multiple [[variable]]s.
# {{context|intransitive|biology|lang=en}} To produce distinct [[organ]]s or to achieve specific functions by a process of [[development]] called [[differentiation]].
#* {{quote-book|title=[[S:Insects, Their Ways and Means of Living|Insects: Their Ways and Means of Living]]|year=1930|author=Robert Evans Snodgrass
|passage=In Chapter IV we learned that every animal consists of a body, or soma, formed of cells that are '''differentiated''' from the germ cells usually at an early stage of development.}}

